1
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:04,900
我们必须告诉他
We have to tell him.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:06,760
希望他没事
I hope he's okay.

3
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:09,820
沃特 我们隔壁的老邻居 过世了
Walt, our elderly next door neighbor, died.

4
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:11,420
他和卢克非常亲近
He and Luke were pretty close,

5
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:12,260
所以我们必须得告诉他
so we have to tell him.

6
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:13,960
我对此有点小紧张
I'm a little nervous about it.

7
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:15,780
我想我们应该循序渐进地告诉他
I think we should break it to him slowly.

8
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:16,600
比如
Like how?

9
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:19,300
第一天我们就说
Well, first we'd say,

10
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:20,880
卢克 你的朋友沃特得了感冒
"Luke, your friend Walt has a cold.

11
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:21,960
你就别去他家了
You shouldn't go over there."

12
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:24,540
第二天就说 不好了 沃特进了医院
Next day--"Bad news. Walt's in the hospital,

13
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,320
不过他还能和护士们谈笑风生
but he's still cracking jokes with the nurses."

14
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:27,920
第三天 他们正尝试使用
Next day--"They're trying

15
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:28,980
一种尚在试验阶段的新药
an experimental drug.

16
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:29,760
但愿他没事
Fingers crossed."

17
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,940
第四天 他产生了排斥反应
Next day--"His body rebelled.

18
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:32,560
陷入了昏迷
He's in a coma."

19
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:35,180
第五天 他醒了 第六天 又昏了
Next day--he rallies, next day--coma,

20
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:36,180
第七天 仍然昏
Next day--coma,

21
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:37,100
第八天 继续昏
next day--coma,

22
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:38,220
第九天 眼皮轻颤
next day--eye flutter--

23
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:40,140
打住 打住 别说了
Stop. Just stop. Stop.

24
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:44,180
卢克 我们不得不告诉你一个坏消息
Oh, Luke, we have some bad news for you.

25
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:45,380
是有关沃特的
It's about Walt.

26
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:48,320
很抱歉
I'm afraid...

27
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:50,980
他去世了
He passed away.

28
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,620
是昨天的事
Um, it happened yesterday.

29
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:56,180
他刚给邮政部长写完了一封
He finished writing an angry letter

30
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:59,340
满怀怒气的信 然后就睡死过去了
to the postmaster general, and he just fell asleep.

31
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:00,480
好吧
Okay.

32
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:02,460
一切都很很平静
It was very peaceful.

33
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:07,520
除了那信 信里全是威胁恐吓 不过
Not the letter. That was full of threats, but...

34
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,180
你伤心也是应该的 宝贝
It's okay to be sad, honey.

35
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:11,400
你们俩是非常好的朋友
You two were really good friends.

36
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,570
听到这消息你一定很震惊吧
It must be quite a shock to hear that...

37
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:15,320
沃特他死了
Walt's dead.

38
00:01:18,338 --> 00:01:21,780
你想和我们谈谈心吗
Um, so do you wanna talk about it or...

39
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:22,360
我没事
I'm okay.

40
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:25,260
我能回去玩游戏了吗 我按了暂停
Can I get back to my video game? It's paused.

41
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:27,680
没问题
Oh, um, sure.

42
00:01:28,020 --> 00:01:28,560
老弟
Yeah, buddy.

43
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:29,840
过来抱抱
Come here.

44
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,080
他的表现也太奇怪了
How weird was that?

45
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:36,380
我知道 太诡异了
I know. Crazy weird.

46
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:39,040
他简直就像是铁石心肠一样
It's like he had no feelings at all.

47
00:01:39,620 --> 00:01:41,320
我倒觉得你的表现比较诡异
I'm more worried about the one you showed.

48
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:42,400
你那微笑是什么意思
What's with all the smiling?

49
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:43,980
你在说什么啊
What are you talking about?

50
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:44,820
你那咧嘴一笑
That grin.

51
00:01:45,047 --> 00:01:47,520
"沃特他死了" 跟蝙蝠侠里小丑似的
"Walt's dead." You looked like the Joker.

52
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:48,340
我才没笑呢
I didn't smile.

53
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:50,440
你笑了 就像是某种怪异的应对机制
You did. It's like a weird coping mechanism.

54
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:52,680
上次你告诉他仓鼠死时也是这幅摸样
You did the same thing when you told him his hamster died.

55
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:56,180
我不知道你以为自己看见了什么 菲尔
I don't know what you thought you saw, Phil,

56
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,400
可我们的儿子刚刚听到了悲惨的消息
but our child just got some terrible news

57
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,980
却表现得平静异常 你对此不担心吗
and had absolutely no reaction. Doesn't that concern you?

58
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:04,840
当然担心 他只是需要时间来消化而已
Yeah. He probably just needs time to process it.

59
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,180
你这么想吗
Do you think?

60
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:07,840
是啊 亲爱的
Yeah, honey.

61
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:10,500
生死离别对任何年纪的人都很难面对
Death is a profound thing to deal with at any age.

62
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:11,780
我们的处理方式各不相同
We all manage it differently.

63
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:15,200
有的人隐藏他们的感受
Some people lock up their feelings.

64
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:15,980
其他人则
Others...

65
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:18,260
转向他人寻求慰藉
reach out for comfort,

66
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:22,260
设法再次确认自己那鲜活的肉体...
finding some way to reaffirm their connection to life--

67
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:23,702
想都别想
You're joking.

68
00:02:38,772 --> 00:02:39,720
你好啊 海莉
Hola, Haley.

69
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:40,820
歌洛莉亚 我开车经过
Gloria, I was driving by

70
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:42,680
看到门外放了报纸 就给你送进来了
and saw this outside your door, so here.

71
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:44,520
-谢了 -不客气
- Thank you. - No problem.

72
00:02:45,340 --> 00:02:47,620
既然我人都来了
Hey, so since I'm already here,

73
00:02:47,620 --> 00:02:50,000
我朋友今晚本来要开一个泳池派对
my friend was gonna have a pool party tonight,

74
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,540
可他生病了 能让我们在这里开吗
but he got sick. Could we have it here?

75
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:55,100
幸好你看到报纸了
Mm. Good thing that you saw this paper

76
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:57,540
不然你永远没机会开口问了
or if not, you would have never been able to ask.

77
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:58,240
说得是啊
Yeah.

78
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:00,319
抱歉 我和杰今晚
I'm sorry, but Jay and I are going

79
00:03:00,319 --> 00:03:02,975
要去米奇和小卡家吃晚饭呢
to Mitch and Cam's for dinner tonight.

80
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:04,780
你就当我自言自语好了
I'm just thinking out loud here.

81
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:07,960
如果有个我父母同意的监护人全程陪同
What if I get a chaperone that my parents approve of?

82
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:08,900
你会答应吗
Would it be okay then?

83
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:10,880
这样的话 行啊
Well, I guess so.

84
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,640
说起来 如果曼尼也能放松一下也不错
You know, it would be good for Manny to have a little bit of fun.

85
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:16,980
你介意他留下来参加派对吗
Do you mind if he stays here for the party?

86
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,860
介意 整个计划都指望他了
Mind? The plan depended on him.

87
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:22,020
你大概没考虑过监护人的问题吧
I don't suppose you've thought of a chaperone?

88
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:23,120
当然没想过 妈妈
Of course not, mom,

89
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,800
因为我的派对将会狂野放荡
because it's going to be a wild party

90
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:26,760
而我也会和往常一样想要逃脱惩罚
and I'm trying to get away with something, as usual.

91
00:03:26,780 --> 00:03:27,900
我当然考虑过监护人的事
Yes, I thought of a chaperone--

92
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:29,640
舅舅已经答应做我的监护人了
My uncle who already said he would do it.

93
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:30,860
如果那样还不行的话
But if that's gonna be a problem,

94
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:31,980
-我就只好打电话通知各位 -抱歉
- I think I should just call everybody-- - sorry.

95
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:33,000
我错了 我批准了
Sorry. Sorry. It's fine.

96
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:35,220
谢谢您啦 曼尼舅舅
And thank you, uncle Manny.

97
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,260
你能不能搭把手啊
Can you help a little bit?

98
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:39,860
如果我按下这里 就会
This--if I--if I push down, does that...

99
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:41,460
好一点了 好一点了
Yeah, that's helping. That's helping.

100
00:03:41,460 --> 00:03:43,216
不 一点都不好 都卡住了
No, it's not helping. It's 'cause it's stuck.

101
00:03:43,216 --> 00:03:44,921
真不敢相信我居然把它卡住了
I can't believe I got 'em this stuck.

102
00:03:44,921 --> 00:03:46,240
我这辈子都在造床
I've built beds my whole life--

103
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,880
双层床 狗狗的床 牛牛的床
Bunk beds, dog beds, cow beds.

104
00:03:47,891 --> 00:03:49,743
我打赌你绝对没造过牛牛的床
Okay, I'm calling you on cow beds.

105
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:51,420
我爸来了
Oh, that's my dad!

106
00:03:51,535 --> 00:03:52,640
太好了 他能帮上忙
Okay. He can help.

107
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:54,480
他造过船 码头 湖泊
He's built a boat, a dock, a lake...

108
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:56,373
他绝对没造过湖泊
Uh, he did not build a lake.

109
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:58,200
从今往后 举例时编到第二个就打住吧
Okay, from now on, just stop after you say the second thing.

110
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:00,760
驾驶舱门打开了
...So the cabin door swings open.

111
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:03,100
飞行员居然是个女的
Damned if there wasn't a lady pilot in there.

112
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,140
你说得对
Yeah, well,

113
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:06,580
我不愿意承认 可是我对此也很不爽
I hate to admit it, but it throws me, too.

114
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:07,960
我还是喜欢男人一点
I do prefer a man.

115
00:04:08,301 --> 00:04:10,286
我们又得就你的取向讨论一番吗
Are we gonna have this conversation again?

116
00:04:10,286 --> 00:04:12,036
-莫尔 -你好吗
- Hey, Merle. - Hey. How are you?

117
00:04:12,036 --> 00:04:13,509
-好吧 -很高兴见到你
- Yeah, ooh. Okay. - Nice to see you.

118
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,640
让我帮你提这个吧
All right, let me grab that for you.

119
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:15,760
不 我自己来就好
No. No. I got it.

120
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:18,600
你如果愿意帮我拿瓶啤酒 那可敢情好
I will take that beer you were about to offer me, though.

121
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:19,380
啤酒马上就来
Oh, yeah. Coming right up.

122
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:21,220
你知道东西都在哪儿 快坐下吧
And you know where everything is. Go have a seat.

123
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:23,900
有个我爸的未接来电呢
Oh, I missed a call from my dad.

124
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,860
让我猜猜 是打来取消晚餐的吧
Oh, let me guess. Is he calling to cancel?

125
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:28,100
这次又是什么借口
What's his excuse this time?

126
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:30,680
你这么想真是小肚鸡肠 小卡
You know, that's a really mean thing to assume, Cam.

127
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,800
你可以不要总是揪着我爸不放吗
I really wish you'd give my dad a break for once.

128
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:34,920
得了吧 你明知道杰不待见我爸
Oh, please. You know Jay doesn't like my dad.

129
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:37,200
他觉得我爸是乡下来的土包子
He thinks he's some bumpkin from the sticks.

130
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,720
我会让你们知道莫尔·斯通沃尔·塔克
Well, I will have you know that Merle Stonewall Tucker

131
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,620
可是全密苏里州最牛逼
is one of the most respected farmers

132
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:43,644
最受人尊敬的农民
in all of hell's hollow, Missouri.

133
00:04:43,644 --> 00:04:46,138
你也不听听你自己说的话
Okay, you're not hearing yourself.

134
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:48,380
我爸并不讨厌你爸 别这样
My dad likes him just fine. Come on.

135
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:52,740
喂 老爸 是我
Hello? Hey, dad. It's me.

136
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:53,540
米奇
Mitch.

137
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,140
我病了
I'm sick.

138
00:04:56,608 --> 00:04:59,034
我今晚来不了了
I gotta cancel tonight.

139
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:02,300
没错没错 6点 期待你们的光临
Yeah. Yeah, 6:00. We're really looking forward to it.

140
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:04,240
你什么意思 我不是说不能来了吗
What are you doing? I just said I can't come.

141
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,240
我不知道 等我问一下
I don't know. Let me ask.

142
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:07,800
我爸问是喝红酒还是白酒
My dad wants to know red or white?

143
00:05:08,105 --> 00:05:09,860
红酒吧
Um, uh, red.

144
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:11,200
红酒吧 是我错了
Red. And I'm sorry.

145
00:05:11,210 --> 00:05:14,006
没事 小卡让带红酒
Okay. Yeah, Cam says red.

146
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:15,960
是的 对 他挺开心的
Okay. Yeah, he's--he's so happy--

147
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:17,880
省省吧 老家伙 我知道你没病
Knock it off, old man. You are not sick.

148
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:18,900
为什么你总是这样
Why do you always do this?

149
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:20,620
听着 咱自家人私底下说
Okay, look, between you and me,

150
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:21,640
我觉得莫维斯人挺烦的
Mervis kind of bugs me.

151
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:23,189
首先 人家叫莫尔
Okay, first of all, it's Merle.

152
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:25,080
莫维斯都不是个名字 只是种声音
Mervis isn't a name. Mervis is a sound.

153
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:27,575
其次 他可是我爱人的爸爸啊
And second of all, he's-- he's my partner's father.

154
00:05:27,575 --> 00:05:29,092
懂没 你必须得来
Okay? You're coming.

155
00:05:29,092 --> 00:05:30,660
老爸 你干嘛不四处转转
Okay, dad, why don't you settle in?

156
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:32,720
杰跟歌洛莉亚来就餐之前 我们没什么安排
We don't have plans until dinner tonight with Jay and Gloria.

157
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:34,360
我不喜欢那家伙
I-I don't like that guy.

158
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:36,320
什么 这...
What? That's--

159
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:37,060
你不对谁都挺好的嘛
You like everybody.

160
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:40,180
除了杰 他有时候让我觉得很烦
Not Jay. The guy rubs me the wrong way.

161
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:42,380
每次我一想 表达我的善意时
Every time I try to do something nice,

162
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:44,180
他都给我摆一张臭脸 就像这样
he makes this cranky face, like...

163
00:05:44,845 --> 00:05:46,530
行了 这样吧
Okay. Well, you know what?

164
00:05:46,530 --> 00:05:48,629
我就当你是时差还没到过来
I'm gonna chalk this up to jet lag

165
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,680
因为这一点都不像你
for you because it's not like you at all.

166
00:05:50,855 --> 00:05:52,580
你得稍微试着接纳他
Okay, you have to make an effort.

167
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:53,720
他可是我爱人的父亲
It's my partner's father.

168
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,285
咆哮一下给我听 就当你同意了
Now give me the growl that means "Okay."

169
00:05:57,916 --> 00:05:58,860
很好
Good.

170
00:05:58,860 --> 00:05:59,940
你知道沃特有个女儿
Did you know Walt had a daughter

171
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:01,620
却和他形同陌路吗
he was completely estranged from?

172
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:05,560
律师说他女儿甚至不愿了却他的遗愿
His lawyer said she wouldn't even honor his last request

173
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:07,380
不肯把他的狗牌扔进大海
to toss his dog tags in the ocean.

174
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:08,260
真是难以置信
Can you imagine?

175
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:10,160
菲尔 真的有必要再谈这茬吗
Phil, do we really have to go through this again?

176
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:12,180
我答应过你 我肯定会尽全力
I told you, I would do everything possible

177
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:13,380
保证把你的骸骨
to make sure that your skeleton

178
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:15,140
贡献给女子大学做科学课堂教材
ends up in a science class at a women's college.

179
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:16,620
不是 只是有些伤感
No, it's just sad.

180
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:19,800
我晚年生活的一半就指着
That's half of what would keep me going in my old age--

181
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:22,080
回忆跟孩子们的幸福时光过活了
remembering all the good times with the kids.

182
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:25,100
教卢克骑自行车
Teaching Luke to ride his bike...

183
00:06:26,380 --> 00:06:28,500
跟海莉跳父女舞
Haley at the father-daughter dance...

184
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:32,540
第一次带艾丽克斯骑小马
Taking Alex for her first pony ride...

185
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:34,400
你从没带她骑过小马
You never took Alex on a pony ride.

186
00:06:35,849 --> 00:06:37,848
哦对 就我一人去的
Oh, right. That was just me.

187
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:39,020
但我带艾丽克斯去了...
But Alex and I went...

188
00:06:39,450 --> 00:06:41,246
不对 那次是带海莉去的
Oh, no. That was Haley.

189
00:06:43,623 --> 00:06:45,747
菲尔 你看 是卢克
Phil, look. It's Luke.

190
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:46,900
他要进沃特家了
He's going into Walt's house.

191
00:06:49,970 --> 00:06:52,259
他这是要去告别一下
Oh, he's saying good-bye.

192
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:54,760
说了他只是需要点时间
He just needed a little time.

193
00:06:55,556 --> 00:06:58,467
真是又感人又感伤
It's so sweet and so sad.

194
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:02,460
他比我想象中有人情味多了
He's so much more sensitive than I ever thought.

195
00:07:03,836 --> 00:07:05,915
他们的关系很特别 要是有天卢克写出
They had a special bond. I wouldn't be surprised

196
00:07:05,915 --> 00:07:08,530
像《相约星期二》那样的书也不奇怪
if one day he wrote a book like "Tuesdays with Morrie".

197
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,180
那本书我倒没读过
I never read it.

198
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:12,802
不过主人公偷了莫里家的电视没
Did that guy steal Morrie's TV?

199
00:07:22,620 --> 00:07:25,200
让我们踏上冒险旅程吧
Now setting a course for adventure!

200
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:30,260
我跟孩子们都有过超棒的回忆
I've had great experiences with all my kids.

201
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:33,780
不过 也许我稍稍冷落艾丽克斯了
But I... I might have fallen behind a bit with Alex.

202
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:35,120
完全是我的责任
My fault completely.

203
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:37,400
还冒险呢 这是要去把狗牌
Adventure? We are throwing dog tags

204
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:38,480
扔到已经饱受污染的海里
into an already polluted ocean

205
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:40,140
搞不好会噎死一只水獭呢
where they will probably choke an otter.

206
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:43,339
就80%是我的责任
80% my fault.

207
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:46,000
亲爱的 我们这是来了结一个人的遗愿
Honey, we're bringing closure to a man's life.

208
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:48,480
我们一会儿爬到能俯瞰大海的高处
We'll hike up to the scenic overlook,

209
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:50,520
据说沃特就在那儿向他的妻子求婚的
where apparently, Walt proposed to his wife,

210
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:53,380
等到光线柔和静谧时 说些悼词
wait for the light to be just right, say a few words,

211
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:54,320
分享一些回忆
share some memories.

212
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:56,037
听起来倒有些诗意
That's kind of poetic.

213
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:57,580
有些纳瓦伙族的味道
Kind of Navajo.

214
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,080
你终于也上道了
Now you're getting it.

215
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,420
我们会让他带着尊严走完这一生
We'll be sending him off with a level of dignity,

216
00:08:01,420 --> 00:08:04,220
幸运的话 我们有天也将体会
that if we're lucky, someday we'll experience, too.

217
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,220
这叫做...
It's called--

218
00:08:21,860 --> 00:08:24,140
这是什么啊 沃特的旧电视吗
Hey. What do you got there? Walt's old TV?

219
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:26,600
他说过他死后我可以挑一件他的东西
He said I could take one thing after he died.

220
00:08:26,609 --> 00:08:28,266
要是两件就好了
I wish he would've said two things.

221
00:08:28,266 --> 00:08:30,385
我还想要那个按键很大的电话
I would've taken that phone with the big buttons.

222
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:34,260
我相信你们一起看电视的时候
I bet you guys had some really good times

223
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:35,420
一定很开心 对吧
watching this thing, right?

224
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:38,148
那倒没有 我屋里刚好差个电视而已
No. I just wanted a tv in my room.

225
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:40,260
听着 卢克
You know, Luke,

226
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:43,460
也许有更好的方法来纪念沃特
there might be a nicer way to honor Walt's memory.

227
00:08:43,700 --> 00:08:44,400
什么意思
What do you mean?

228
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:47,834
比如说 你们喜欢一起打理花园
Well, I mean, you guys liked to garden.

229
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:50,340
我们可以从他的花园挑一枝花
We could, uh, we could take one of his flowers

230
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:53,620
栽到咱家院子里 每当春天到来时
and plant it in our yard, and then every spring, when--

231
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:56,160
这样就好了
There we go.

232
00:08:58,700 --> 00:09:00,560
亲爱的 你心里什么滋味
Sweetie, how are you feeling?

233
00:09:01,382 --> 00:09:03,900
难过 还是生气
You sad? Angry?

234
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:05,280
困惑 还是沮丧
Confused? Frustrated?

235
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:07,365
你有什么想法都可以跟我说
You know you can talk to me.

236
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:09,740
知道啦 你挡着电视了 快闪开行吗
I know, but I can't see through you. Could you scootch?

237
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:12,860
不行 这样可不行
No. No. You know, this is not okay.

238
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:13,760
我要把它送回去
It's going back.

239
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,860
什么 他说我可以挑一件的
What? He said I could pick one thing.

240
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:16,700
这不叫挑
This isn't picking.

241
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:18,420
这叫抢 我要送回去了
It's looting, and it's going back.

242
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:20,400
你真是个坏女人
You are so mean.

243
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:22,380
那会儿沃特经常拿望远镜偷看你
When Walt used to look through those binoculars

244
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:25,740
还说什么"你爸真是好福气" 他错了
and say, "Your dad's one lucky man", he was wrong.

245
00:09:28,261 --> 00:09:28,876
嗨 海莉
Hi, Haley.

246
00:09:28,876 --> 00:09:31,440
嗨 斯蒂芬 山姆 这是曼尼
Hi. Stef, Sam, this is Manny.

247
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:31,960
你好啊 老兄
What's up, dude?

248
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,360
厨房在那边 泳池在后面
Kitchen's over there and pool's in the back.

249
00:09:34,020 --> 00:09:35,040
你爸妈没来吗
So where are your parents?

250
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:35,800
他们不来
They're not coming.

251
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:37,480
我妈说会有监护人到场的啊
I was told there'd be a chaperone.

252
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:39,220
有啊 就是你
There is. It's you.

253
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:41,220
我爸妈觉得没问题
My parents are totally fine with it.

254
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,000
我想想 安全出口
Well, exits,

255
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:45,200
灭火器 烧伤药箱
fire extinguisher, burn kit.

256
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,220
都齐全 来找点乐子吧
Okay, let's have some fun.

257
00:09:47,572 --> 00:09:50,520
我相信我说得很明白 禁入卧室
I believe I was clear the bedrooms were off-limits.

258
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:52,280
小姑娘 送你一句箴言
Young lady, I don't think you're ready up here

259
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:53,560
张腿先过脑 开窍不开苞
for what you're planning to do up there.

260
00:09:57,501 --> 00:09:59,482
在我眼皮底下别想
Ugh. Not on my watch.

261
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:04,440
菜做得真美味啊 米奇尔
Oh, this was a delicious meal, Mitchell.

262
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:07,840
要是我老婆厨艺这么棒就好了
I wish my wife could cook a roast like this.

263
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:09,840
你是好福气啊 儿子
You got a good one there, son.

264
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:12,140
没错 我的福分 就像你跟妈妈一样
Oh, well, I'm very lucky, just like you and mama.

265
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:13,760
幸福美满一辈子
Never had a bad patch.

266
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:15,920
除了1985年冬天的那次 还记得吗
Except the winter of '85. Remember that?

267
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:19,400
那可不 那几晚我只好睡牛床上了
Oh, I spent several nights in the cow bed then.

268
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,440
来来来 我帮你收拾
Oh, here. Let me help you.

269
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:25,065
不用不用 你坐下
No, no, no. You sit--sit down.

270
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:28,400
我们男人们来叙叙旧
Let--lets us guys catch up here a little bit.

271
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:30,340
告诉你们我很烦那人的原因吧
I'll tell you why I don't like that guy--

272
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:31,600
我是不会跟米奇尔说的
and I could never say this to Mitch--

273
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:34,040
他把我儿子当做女人一样对待
He treats my son like the wife in the relationship.

274
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:35,040
一直都这样
Always has.

275
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:39,040
吃甜点前 我要送些礼物给你们
Before we get to dessert, I've got some presents here.

276
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:41,080
不用这么客气啦 老爸
Oh, you didn't need to, dad.

277
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,460
大爱啊
Love it!

278
00:10:44,260 --> 00:10:47,020
哇 莫尔 真是太谢谢你了
Oh, Merle, thank you so much.

279
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:50,180
瞧瞧这个 真是典雅大方
Look at this. Oh. So elegant, huh?

280
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:52,240
真是太贴心了
Oh, this is so sweet.

281
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:53,640
感动得快哭出来了
I think I might cry.

282
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:54,120
千万别
Don't.

283
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:56,980
老爸 我真的要回家了
Dad, I really gotta get home.

284
00:10:56,980 --> 00:10:59,140
我知道 我知道 你要做作业
I know. I know. You gotta do homework.

285
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:01,860
但是当你看到一个牌子上写着
But you can't expect me to see a sign that says,

286
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:04,100
"世间绝迹之美味奶昔 前50英里"
"World's greatest milk shake--50 miles,"

287
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:05,460
怎能不驱车前往呢
and not drive to it.

288
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:07,440
对不起两位 机器坏了
Sorry, sweetie. Machine's broken.

289
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:11,000
我就是想和我家闺女度过特别的一天
I just wanted a special day with my daughter,

290
00:11:11,220 --> 00:11:14,140
比如"我们在海滩上给一位老人
You know, like "the time we gave an old man

291
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:16,236
办了场意义非凡的送别仪式"
a dramatic sendoff at the beach,"

292
00:11:16,284 --> 00:11:18,807
或者"有次我们开了100英里
or--or "the time we drove 100 miles

293
00:11:18,807 --> 00:11:20,874
去吃世界上最美味的奶昔"
for the world's greatest milk shake."

294
00:11:21,340 --> 00:11:22,720
要生的时候给我们电话 弗朗辛
Call us when it happens, Francine.

295
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,600
你们到家前我说不定就要生了
Oh, it could be before you get home.

296
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,620
预产期已经过了一周了
I'm a week past my due date as it is.

297
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:28,420
要吃点什么吗
What can I do for you?

298
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:31,500
"有次我们帮忙接生了个孩子"
"The time we delivered a baby."

299
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:34,520
那儿除了她就是我们了 她又快生了
We were the only ones there, and she was so close,

300
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:36,540
一根针掉到地上的声音都能起到催生作用
The sound of a pin dropping could induce labor.

301
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:38,620
好
Okay!

302
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:41,160
吃什么好呢
What looks good?

303
00:11:41,260 --> 00:11:42,800
吃什么好呢
What looks good?

304
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:44,480
吃什么好呢
What looks good?

305
00:11:51,014 --> 00:11:55,380
孩子都爱搞破坏
Wh-whoa! Kids love to destroy things.

306
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:57,340
曼尼不这样 他一直都太一本正经了
Not Manny. He's always been a little bit too serious.

307
00:11:57,700 --> 00:12:00,920
一般我负责造房子 他就负责来验收
I would make the buildings, and he would inspect them.

308
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:04,320
一旦哪里不合法规 各种批文就来了
And if they weren't up to code, ay, ay, ay, the paperwork.

309
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:07,080
我记得小卡有一次
I remember Cam, one time,

310
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:09,380
把拖拉机轮胎滚进了鸡窝
rolled a tractor tire right through a chicken coop.

311
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:11,590
他那时候才3岁
He was 3 at the time.

312
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:14,140
我记得米奇尔有一次
I remember Mitchell, one time,

313
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:15,720
空手劈向一块厚玻璃板
karate-chopped a plate glass window.

314
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:17,060
缝了17针
Got 17 stitches.

315
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:18,712
我爱死这个故事了
Ah, yes. I love that story.

316
00:12:18,712 --> 00:12:21,262
他扮演的是霹雳娇娃[女]中的哪一个来着
Which one of the Charlie's angels he was being again?

317
00:12:21,272 --> 00:12:23,700
-那不重要 -我觉得是费拉
- That's not important. - I think it was Farrah.

318
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:26,720
对 我记得米奇尔讲那个故事的时候
Yeah, the thing I remember is, when Mitchell told that story,

319
00:12:26,733 --> 00:12:28,180
一直在咯咯笑
how--how he giggled all the way through.

320
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:28,920
我想他没有在咯咯笑
I'm sure he wasn't giggling.

321
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:31,451
他绝对在咯咯笑
Oh, yeah, he--he was giggling, all right.

322
00:12:32,902 --> 00:12:34,833
不 米奇尔通常都是爆笑
No, see, Mitchell has a booming laugh.

323
00:12:34,833 --> 00:12:36,960
卡梅隆才是那个喜欢尖声笑的
It's Cameron, actually-- has the high laugh.

324
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:38,380
像是
You know...

325
00:12:39,144 --> 00:12:41,167
不 我觉得米奇的笑声更尖
No, I think Mitch has a higher laugh than--

326
00:12:41,167 --> 00:12:42,201
是这样
It's...

327
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:44,220
不 是这样
No, it's...

328
00:12:49,452 --> 00:12:50,020
听听他俩
Listen to them.

329
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:51,280
听听他俩
Listen to them.

330
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:52,080
好哥俩啊这是
Best of friends.

331
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:54,860
亲爱的 我很抱歉我那么说杰
Oh, man. I'm sorry I doubted Jay.

332
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:55,960
他很贴心
He's been lovely.

333
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:57,601
好吧 真心话时间
Oh, well, confession time--

334
00:12:57,601 --> 00:12:59,682
他确实有点不想来
He kinda didn't want to come.

335
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:02,800
听到这个你一定很想笑
Well, you're gonna laugh

336
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:05,692
因为我爸也有点希望他不要来
because my dad was kinda hoping he wouldn't.

337
00:13:05,692 --> 00:13:07,277
什么
Wha?

338
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:09,920
他们只是需要多互相了解一下
Oh. They just needed to get to know one another better.

339
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:11,420
我真高兴我们做到了
I am so glad that we did this.

340
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:12,220
我也很高兴
Yeah, me, too.

341
00:13:14,399 --> 00:13:15,374
说来有趣
Oh, that's so funny.

342
00:13:15,374 --> 00:13:17,400
你爸为什么不喜欢我爸
Wh-what did your dad not like about my dad?

343
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:19,520
你知道杰的 他可爱得很
Oh, well, you know Jay. He's a teddy bear,

344
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:22,280
但有时候 他总以一副硬汉冷面孔示人
but sometimes he can kinda come off as a tough guy.

345
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:23,560
那倒是真的
Yeah, that's true.

346
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:25,420
作为一个真正的硬汉
As an actual tough guy,

347
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:27,860
你就能理解为什么我爸会被惹到了
You can kinda see how that would rub my dad the wrong way.

348
00:13:30,269 --> 00:13:31,980
那个...我看得出来 不过
Oh, it's--I-I could see that, but, you know,

349
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:34,260
我爸其实真是个硬汉 所以...
my dad's actually pretty tough himself, so...

350
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:35,520
是吗 都市硬汉而已
Oh, yeah, city tough,

351
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:38,140
而不是 乡野硬汉
You know, not farm tough.

352
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:41,120
你说的都市 是指黑帮遍布的那种吧
You mean cities, where there are gangs,

353
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:44,815
乡野可就不一样了 遍布的都是小鸭子
as to opposed to farms, where there are ducks?

354
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:48,100
天呐 里面卡得死死的
Oh, boy. It's really jammed in there.

355
00:13:48,113 --> 00:13:50,320
老爸 要不你过去搭把手吧
Yeah. Why don't you hop on in there, dad?

356
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:51,040
我爸能搞定
My dad's got it.

357
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:53,400
-好 我来看看 -坚持住 莫尔
- All right, let's see here. - Hang on, Merle.

358
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,484
-等等 这里吗 -撑住 好
- Wait. Here. Huh? - Hold. Yeah, that's good.

359
00:13:56,116 --> 00:13:56,748
快出来了
Oh. It's coming.

360
00:13:56,748 --> 00:13:57,775
我们能搞定 我们能搞定
We got it. We got it.

361
00:13:57,785 --> 00:13:59,740
这就对了 这就对了
Oh, there you go. There you go.

362
00:13:59,740 --> 00:14:01,780
小卡 帮我们拿点冰饮来吧
Cam, why don't you go get us a couple of cold ones?

363
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:04,140
这边交给我们就行了
We'll finish this job up in here.

364
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:05,860
当然 老爸 应该的
Sure thing, dad. You earned it.

365
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:07,920
对 谢谢帮忙 莫尔
Yeah. Good helping there, Merle. Okay.

366
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,100
这里面真热
It's hot in here.

367
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:14,200
有80华氏度吧[27摄氏度左右]
It's, like, 80 degrees.

368
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:16,480
他这么做是让外卖女郎
He did that so the meals on wheels lady

369
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:17,620
不得不宽衣解带
had to take off her sweater.

370
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:19,060
这儿灯是怎么开的
How do we turn on the lights in here?

371
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:21,040
可不是嘛
Of course.

372
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:25,220
卢克 既然我们到这儿了
So, Luke, now that we're here,

373
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:28,340
要不你就跟我说说沃特对你有多重要
you wanna take a minute and say what Walt meant to you?

374
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:29,040
不想说
Nope.

375
00:14:30,460 --> 00:14:32,920
卢克 你正经历漫漫人生路上的重要一课
Luke, you are going through something huge in your life,

376
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:34,900
我担心你没能以一种
and I'm concerned that you're not processing it

377
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:37,000
恰当的方式去处理
in a normal, healthy way.

378
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,540
我伤心 我特别非常地伤心
I'm sad. I'm so very sad.

379
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:41,491
别 你别说这些来应付我
No, I don't just wanna hear what you think I wanna hear.

380
00:14:41,491 --> 00:14:43,152
-我希望你敞开心扉... -你们好
- I want you to really tell me-- - Hi.

381
00:14:43,152 --> 00:14:45,060
我是来来送餐的金姆
It's Kim with meals on wheels.

382
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:46,460
卢克 沃特在哪里
Hi, Luke. Where's Walt?

383
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:49,042
热得跟蒸桑拿一样 他怎么受得了
It is like a sauna in here. How does he stand it?

384
00:14:49,042 --> 00:14:51,965
沃特 我在等我的每日一抱
Walt! I'm waiting for my hug!

385
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:57,520
关于沃特 我有个不幸的消息
I have some sad news about Walt.

386
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:00,820
他去世了
He's dead.

387
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:01,600
什么
What?

388
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:03,300
昨晚去世的
He died last night.

389
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:04,500
你在开玩笑吧
Are you joking?

390
00:15:04,740 --> 00:15:06,900
不 他是心脏病去世的
No. He had a heart attack.

391
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:08,980
有人去世了 你却 你还笑得出来
A man died. You're-- you're smiling.

392
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:09,740
我没在笑
I'm not smiling.

393
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:11,327
撒谎 老妈 吓死个人哦
You are, mom. It's kinda creepy.

394
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:13,682
有人在吗 沃特
Well, hello? Walt?

395
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:15,760
发生什么了
What's going on?

396
00:15:16,089 --> 00:15:17,546
沃特怎么了
Something happen to Walt?

397
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,680
我想你可以猜到的
Well, I'm sure you can imagine.

398
00:15:20,733 --> 00:15:21,991
他病了吗
He sick?

399
00:15:22,780 --> 00:15:23,960
他现在在医院吗
He's in the hospital?

400
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:26,620
天啊 没卖关子了
Oh, my god. Just tell me.

401
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:28,658
好吧
Mm! Okay.

402
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,420
他去世了
He is... dead.

403
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:33,100
-真的吗 -对 他去世了
- He is? - Yeah, he's dead.

404
00:15:33,420 --> 00:15:34,720
你捂着个嘴做什么
What are you doing with your mouth?

405
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:37,620
-没什么 -她在笑 她觉得很滑稽
- Nothing. - She's smiling. She thinks it's funny.

406
00:15:37,700 --> 00:15:39,100
我没有 我没觉得很滑稽
I don't. I don't think it's funny.

407
00:15:39,260 --> 00:15:40,760
-我没在笑 -我不会把这个留给你的
- I'm not smiling. - I'm not leaving this with you.

408
00:15:40,820 --> 00:15:42,360
抱歉 我很抱歉
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

409
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:43,960
我也才知道我脸有这毛病
I just found out my face does this.

410
00:15:44,820 --> 00:15:46,300
老妈 你这样是大不敬啊
Wow, mom. That was so wrong.

411
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:49,995
这只是应对机制的不同 卢克
Well, it's--it's called a coping mechanism, Luke.

412
00:15:49,995 --> 00:15:51,692
有些人会选择压抑自己的情感
Some people repress their feelings

413
00:15:51,692 --> 00:15:55,200
有些人则会选择微笑 不说了越描越黑
and some people just smile. But d--it doesn't matter.

414
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:56,820
把电视机放回小屋去 赶紧离开这儿
Just put the TV in the den. Let's get out of here.

415
00:15:57,020 --> 00:15:58,120
电视机不是放在小屋的
It doesn't go in the den.

416
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:01,480
应该放在这儿
It goes right here.

417
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,520
从我的房间就能看见它了
I can see it from my room.

418
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:08,820
有时候大半夜 我醒来时
Sometimes I'd wake up in the middle of the night

419
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:09,820
往这边一瞧
and look down here.

420
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:12,920
看电视机开着 就知道他还没睡
If the tv was on, I knew he was up,

421
00:16:14,412 --> 00:16:15,551
我也说不清
and I don't know,

422
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:17,480
我想我会怀念这种感觉的
I guess I'm gonna miss that.

423
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:21,680
这真是...
Yeah. That's...

424
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:21,900
是啊
Yeah.

425
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:28,800
好点了吗
Is that any better?

426
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:31,840
还是有那么点儿 摇摇晃晃的
Yeah, it still feels just, you know, a little wobbly.

427
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:33,710
我的天 不不
Oh! Oh, my god. Okay, no, no, no.

428
00:16:33,710 --> 00:16:36,760
没事 没关系 谢谢你 谢谢你
That's--that's fine. Thank you. Thank you.

429
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:39,300
好吧 看样子是时候了
Okay, it's "Go" Time.

430
00:16:40,991 --> 00:16:42,598
好啊 医生
Oh, hey, doc.

431
00:16:44,018 --> 00:16:45,886
没事的 阵痛而已
It's okay. It's just a cramp.

432
00:16:45,886 --> 00:16:47,640
你们还要点些别的吗
Can I get you guys anything else?

433
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:48,960
可千万别 他已经让我吃遍
Please, no. He's already made me eat

434
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:50,800
菜单上"世间绝迹"的各种美食了
the world's greatest everything on the menu.

435
00:16:52,580 --> 00:16:54,240
老爸 你今天怎么这么诡异
Dad, why are you acting like this?

436
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:55,700
是跟沃特去世有关吗
Is this about Walt dying?

437
00:16:55,940 --> 00:16:59,220
不 与他在世时没来得及做的事有关
No. It's about what he didn't do when he was alive--

438
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:01,700
他没能和女儿共创特殊的美好回忆
Have a special bond with his daughter.

439
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:02,960
我不想成为他那样的一个父亲
I don't want to be that kind of dad.

440
00:17:03,020 --> 00:17:04,040
要做就做尤金·塞尔南那样的
I want to be Eugene Cernan.

441
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:05,300
尤金·塞尔南是谁
Who's Eugene Cernan?

442
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:06,960
阿波罗17号的宇航员
"Apollo 17" Astronaut,

443
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:09,240
月上最后一人 史上最酷的爹
Last man on the moon, coolest dad of all time.

444
00:17:10,080 --> 00:17:11,500
他离开月球时 他俯下身去
When he was leaving the moon, he reached down

445
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:13,880
把他女儿名字的缩写 刻在了月球表面
and wrote his daughter's initials into the lunar surface.

446
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:15,220
由于月球上没有空气流动
Since there's no atmosphere--

447
00:17:15,309 --> 00:17:17,052
所以它会永远留在那
There'll be there forever.

448
00:17:18,260 --> 00:17:20,620
所以每次当她仰望天空时
Wow. So every time she looks in the sky,

449
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:22,280
就能收到那专属于她的讯息
she knows there's a message just for her.

450
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:25,280
没错 全世界的爹都恨尤金·塞尔南
Exactly. That's why dads everywhere hate Eugene Cernan.

451
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:26,860
不是吧
Oh, no.

452
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:29,704
好吧 "恨"这字眼确实重了 只是
Okay, "Hate's" A strong word. It's just--

453
00:17:29,716 --> 00:17:31,340
我是想说
I'm trying to make--

454
00:17:31,340 --> 00:17:33,060
天啊
Oh. Oh, boy.

455
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:35,003
亲爱的
Honey. Okay.

456
00:17:35,003 --> 00:17:35,880
我是真想帮你
I really wanna help,

457
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:37,360
不过都说见别人打哈欠或呕吐时
but you know when someone yawns,

458
00:17:37,440 --> 00:17:38,360
自己也会有反应
It makes you yawn?

459
00:17:39,105 --> 00:17:40,631
你也想吐了 是吗
You're not gonna yawn, are you?

460
00:17:40,631 --> 00:17:44,788
都已经到嗓子眼了 天哪
I already yawned a little in my mouth. Oh, god.

461
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:47,460
杰 帮了这么大忙 真得谢谢你
Jay, I want to thank you for helping me do this.

462
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:51,360
小卡肯定很开心 不用自己一人忙活了
I know Cam appreciates not having to do it all on his own.

463
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:55,740
怎么 摆什么臭脸呢
What? What's that face?

464
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:56,700
你真想知道
You really wanna know?

465
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:57,060
当然
Sure.

466
00:17:59,260 --> 00:18:01,200
有时候我觉得 在他们的关系中
Sometimes I think you treat my son

467
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:02,500
你把我儿子当成女人
like the woman in their relationship.

468
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:04,400
-什么 -比如那对表
- What? - Like those watches.

469
00:18:05,340 --> 00:18:07,260
小卡那块又大又爷们
Cam's was all big and manly.

470
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:09,200
另一只看起来
The other one looked like something

471
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:10,540
就像是格蕾丝·凯莉的表
Grace Kelly would wear.

472
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:11,860
那是因为
Well, that's just because

473
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:15,160
米奇的手腕比小卡的要纤细 仅此而已
Mitch has a more slender wrist than cam does. That's all.

474
00:18:15,180 --> 00:18:16,440
他那是瘦 不是纤细
It's skinny, not slender.

475
00:18:16,940 --> 00:18:18,620
那你老老实实告诉我
And you're honestly telling me

476
00:18:18,620 --> 00:18:20,920
你没把米奇放在类似女人的角色中
you don't cast mitch in the more ladylike role?

477
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:23,240
你是说小卡扮演的是老婆的角色吗
Are you saying Cam is the wife in this deal?

478
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:24,200
我没那么想过
I don't think about it that way.

479
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:25,800
现在可不像我们当年那样了
It's not like it was in our day.

480
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:27,140
出门养家糊口的是老公
Husband went out to work.

481
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:28,740
在家相夫教子的是老婆
Wife stayed home with the kids.

482
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,380
真会说话 拐弯抹角地说小卡是女人呗
That sounds like a clever way of saying "Yes."

483
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:32,060
好吧
Fine.

484
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:35,380
他们是平等的
They're both equal.

485
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:37,760
没有谁是女方
Neither one is the wife.

486
00:18:39,620 --> 00:18:40,540
对 对
Yeah. Yeah.

487
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:42,020
我其实也很明白
I know that in my head.

488
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:46,320
只是当我觉得跟他相守一生的人
It's just that it makes me feel a tiny bit better

489
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:49,760
其实有那么一点像女人时
to think that the person he's spending his life with

490
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:52,540
我心里会好过些
is a tiny bit of a woman.

491
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:55,460
我懂的
I get it.

492
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:59,520
每次我对这事刚能接受一点时
Every time I start to feel comfortable with this thing,

493
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:02,100
就又会有新的事情发生让我烦心
some new part comes up I gotta wrap my head around.

494
00:19:02,666 --> 00:19:05,240
事已至此 坦然接受吧
Yeah, I guess we got no choice.

495
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:07,260
对 我们都有两个儿子
Yep. We got two sons,

496
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:09,980
都为对方的基情所倾倒
and they're gay for each other.

497
00:19:11,446 --> 00:19:13,429
回家路上我会慢点开的
I'll take it slow on the way home.

498
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:16,540
别担心 冒险旅程取消
Don't worry. Canceling course for adventure.

499
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:20,040
你猜什么将永存我心难以忘记
You know what I'll never forget?

500
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:22,620
就是我爸花了一整天
The time my dad spent the entire day

501
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:25,460
就为了要给我制造些特殊的回忆
trying to create a special memory for me.

502
00:19:29,220 --> 00:19:31,660
还有 有个孕妇踩着我的呕吐物滑到了
Or when a pregnant lady slipped in my vomit.

503
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:35,440
等着
Hang on.

504
00:19:37,256 --> 00:19:39,215
走之前我得做件事
I wanna do one thing before we go.

505
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:42,460
你在回家路上了吗
Hey, you on your way home?

506
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:45,400
快了 你那边怎么样了
Just about. How's everything there?

507
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:52,360
事实上 一切进展顺利
Actually, it's pretty great.

508
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:54,880
我等不及要见你了
I can't wait to see you.

509
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:56,020
我也是
Me, too.

510
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:57,900
好的
Okay.

511
00:20:00,059 --> 00:20:01,261
走吧
Let's hit it.

512
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:03,660
要不然
I don't know.

513
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:07,740
回家路上我们买点吃的带回去吧
I feel like maybe we should get some food on the way home.

514
00:20:07,940 --> 00:20:08,500
可别
Don't.

515
00:20:10,804 --> 00:20:12,680
来个金枪鱼三明治
Maybe a nice tuna melt.

516
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:13,140
别说了
Stop it.

517
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:27,780
我已经尽力了妈妈 简直跟噩梦一样
I did what I could, mom. It was a nightmare.

518
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:30,540
我都不知道我关了多少次浴室的灯
I can't tell you how many times I turned off the bathroom light.

519
00:20:30,551 --> 00:20:32,231
海莉
Haley!

520
00:20:33,405 --> 00:20:34,880
糟了 听我说 歌洛莉亚
Oh, crap. Listen, Gloria.

521
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:37,780
我之前对你讲的 严格说不算是...
Okay, everything I told you technically was not--

522
00:20:37,780 --> 00:20:38,740
你对我撒谎
You lied to me

523
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:41,080
就为了没人管 为所欲为地开派对
so that you could have a party without supervision!

524
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:43,580
今天晚上管事的还真不少
Oh, I had plenty of supervision.

525
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:46,380
他整晚都拿着杯垫和吸尘器跑来跑去
He was running around all night with his coasters and vacuum

526
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:48,230
义正言辞地教育别人要"做正确的决定"
and his "Make good choices" Speech.

527
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:50,320
很好 总得有个人有点责任心吧
Good. Somebody needed to be responsible.

528
00:20:50,440 --> 00:20:51,000
谢谢
Thank you.

529
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:53,260
没说你 你太一本正经 太刻板了
Not you. You take rules too seriously.

530
00:20:53,560 --> 00:20:54,420
倒成我错了
I'm in trouble?

531
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:55,580
你才13岁
You are 13.

532
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:58,060
你不应该在派对上用吸尘器打扫
You're not supposed to be vacuuming the party.

533
00:20:58,060 --> 00:21:00,440
你应该享受这个派对才是
You're supposed to be enjoying the party.

534
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:01,400
就是嘛
Exactly.

535
00:21:01,620 --> 00:21:03,640
而你压根不应该参加这样的派对
A party that you shouldn't have been having!

536
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:05,569
似乎你的逻辑有点混乱
It seems like you're sending mixed signals here.

537
00:21:05,569 --> 00:21:07,640
也许我应该叫朋友们都走了
Yeah, maybe I should get my friends and just leave.

538
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:09,500
不 你麻烦大了 小姑娘
No, you're in trouble, little young lady.

539
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:10,860
这派对不能停
You're having this party!

540
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:13,280
什么 他们在泳池边用玻璃餐具
What? They've been using glassware by the pool,

541
00:21:13,420 --> 00:21:14,560
把脚放在家具上
putting feet on the furniture,

542
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:16,000
还求女生互相亲对方
and begging girls to kiss each other.

543
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:18,760
对 这些事就是你应该干的
Yes! All the things that you should have been doing!

544
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:21,240
对 这些都没问题
Yeah, all those things are fine.

545
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:23,820
去吧 去好好玩 疯一疯
Go. Have fun and go crazy.

546
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:26,060
他会毁了我的派对的
But he's gonna ruin my party.

547
00:21:26,060 --> 00:21:27,980
一石二鸟 一箭双雕
Two birds with one bullet.
